<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47735" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλασσα</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[θᾰ]</span>, 
			Att.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θά̆λᾰμ-ττα</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12.57
		</span></i> (but <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλασσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					22.236
				</span></i>
			(<i><span class="en">
				338
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i> B.C.)), ἡ: —<i>sea</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.294
			</span></i>, etc.: freq. of the Mediterranean <i>sea</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥδε ἡ θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				185
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.39
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ παρ᾽ ἡμῖν θ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				113a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ θ. ἡ καθ᾽ ἡμᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.3.9
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἐντὸς καὶ κ. ἡ. λεγομένη
			θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				2.5.18
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἔσω θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				393b29
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἔξω θ</span>., of the Ocean,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				350a22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ἀτλαντικὴ θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				392b22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ μεγάλη θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				73
			</span></i>; of a <i>salt lake</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				351a9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς θάλασσαν τὴν τοῦ Εὐξείνου πόντου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.33
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλαγος θαλάσσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.608
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ θάλασσαν</span> by
			<i>sea</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεζῇ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.63
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ γῆς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.28
			</span></i> codd.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατά τε γῆν καὶ κατὰ
			θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Mx.</u>
				241a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χέρσον καὶ θ. ἐκπερῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					240
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς θ. ἀνθεκτέα ἐστί</span>
			one must engage in <i>maritime affairs</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.93
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ περὶ τὴν θ</span>.
			<i>sea</i>-faring men, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				598b24
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1291b20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. καὶ πῦρ καὶ γυνὴ—τρίτον
					κακόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Mon.</u>
					231
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				264
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶν θ</span>
			<i>a sea</i> of troubles, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				758
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Κρὴς τὴν θ</span>.
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγνοεῖ</span>), of pretended
			ignorance, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>sea-water</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστω ἐν χαλκῷ ἡ
			θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				427
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Diph.Siph.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.121d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Moschio
			</span></i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.208a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				16.5.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.83
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>well of salt water</i>, said to be produced by a stroke of  Poseidon's trident, in the Acropolis at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.55
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. Ἐρεχθηΐς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Apollod.
					3.14.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>channel</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>3 Ki.</u>
				18.32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκῆ θ</span>. <i>laver</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ki.</u>
				8.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. κοίλη</span> wooden <i>theatre</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.Gr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				208
			</span></i> (= <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				864
			</span></i>).—For the 
				Lacon.
			 form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάλασσα</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαλασσομέδων</span>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
